    "notes": "Standard-gauge CFS coastal line; connects to the trunk at Homs (via Akkari) and to Aleppo.  [established] The ports were connected inland by rail to Al Akkari (1968) and Aleppo (1975); the coastal TARTUS-LATAKIA link itself opened in 1992. Soviet-assisted CFS expansion.",
    "history": "A standard-gauge (1,435 mm) coastal line serving the ports of Latakia and Tartus, built during the Soviet-assisted CFS expansion: Tartus reached Al Akkari (toward Homs) in 1968 and Latakia reached Aleppo in 1975; the Tartus-Latakia coastal link opened in 1992.",
